  <h1>The Brain as an Interaction Network &amp; Exact Neural Co-Processors</h1>
  <p class="lede">A nervous system has no global clock, no central address bus, and no floating-point coordinator. From ion channels across a lipid bilayer to closed-loop brain–machine co-processors, neural computation is a local, concurrent <strong>interaction network</strong> of active pairs — and its safety, stability, and interpretability admit exact algebraic closure.</p>

  <div class="kg-hint">
    <span>◈ Every pink-underlined <code>term</code> or <code>module.hypercubical</code> below opens its live source &amp; dependency graph from the Hyperactivity store.</span>
    <a href="/kg?mod=neuro/lyapunov.hypercubical">Explore neuro/ in /kg →</a>
  </div>

  <div class="arc-nav">
    <a class="arc-step" href="#part1"><b>Part I · 101</b><span>Excitable Membranes &amp; Local Synaptic Interaction Nets</span></a>
